From 255abb1d8718cdd061c1a6bdbdd55c664797703a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jgrizon
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:09:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shader: prototype explicit LOD for the AGX get_num_mip_levels
 failure

D3DMetal on AGX M1 fails one mesh pipeline with "Encountered unlowered
function call to air.get_num_mip_levels_": its calculateLod lowering asks the
texture for its mip count. With VICTORY_PS_LOD_EXPLICIT=1 a 2D pixel shader's
image_get_lod computes the level itself: 0.5 log2 of the longer
coarse-derivative length in level-0 texels, from getDimensions(h, 0), clamped
to 0..15. The two result channels keep their meaning (clamped, unclamped).
Cubes, a16 and other stages keep calculateLod. Off by default; the switch is
part of the shader cache key.

Ported from paveledits/ScarlettMac runtime-preview/checkpoint/patches/0012-shader-prototype-explicit-LOD-for-the-AGX-get_num_mi.patch

Generated by Mistral Vibe.
Co-Authored-By: Mistral Vibe <vibe@mistral.ai>
